{#
    The other footer: a site's, rather than a surface's.

    The columns are the site itself — the top level of the toctree, a column
    per section, and under each of them the pages it holds. Written out by hand
    they were a second copy of the tree that no check could see going stale: a
    page added under a section reaches the rail and the breadcrumb by itself,
    and the footer kept whatever somebody typed the day it was written.

    Two levels, and no deeper. A section and its pages is a footer; a section,
    its pages and their sections is the sitemap, and a reader who wants that
    wants a page, not the end of every page.

    A page that stands directly under the root is not a section and does not
    get a column to itself — it joins the site's own, the one carrying the
    product's name. A column whose heading and only entry say the same word
    twice is a column saying it once, and three of them in a row read as a
    fault in the renderer.

    `soul.footer.groups` is what the tree cannot know — a licence, a product
    site, somewhere else entirely — and those columns follow the site's own.
    Everything else here is configuration too; see `SoulExtension`. With
    nothing configured and no tree this is the mark and the note, which is the
    least a page can say and still be honest about what it is.
#}
{#- A link inside the project is a *document*, not a path: `/frontend`
    resolves per page, while `frontend.html` resolves from wherever the reader
    happens to be standing and lands in nothing one directory down. A menu
    entry that carries a URL is somebody else's site and is left alone.

    `#` is what the renderer answers for the page being rendered — its way of
    saying "you are here". The footer lists every page of a site, so one of
    them is the reader's own on most pages, and it says so rather than looking
    like a link that goes nowhere. -#}
{%- macro entry(url, label, external) -%}
    {%- set href = external ? url : renderLink(url) -%}
    <a class="sds-link{% if external %} sds-link--external{% endif %}"
       href="{{ href }}"
       {%- if external %} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"{% endif %}
       {%- if href == '#' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ label }}</a>
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- import _self as footer -%}
<footer class="sds-footer">
    {%- set groups = soul.footer.groups is defined ? soul.footer.groups : [] %}
    {%- set entries = [] %}
    {%- for menu in env.projectNode.globalMenues %}
        {%- set entries = entries|merge(menu.menuEntries) %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- set pages = entries|filter(entry => entry.children|default([]) is empty) %}
    {%- set sections = entries|filter(entry => entry.children|default([]) is not empty) %}

    {%- if entries or groups %}
        <div class="sds-footer__groups">
            {%- if pages %}
                <div class="sds-footer__group">
                    <div class="sds-label">{{ soul.product|default(env.projectNode.title)|default('') }}</div>
                    <div class="sds-footer__links">
                        {%- for page in pages %}
                            {{ footer.entry(page.url, page.value.toString, '://' in page.url) }}
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- for section in sections %}
                <div class="sds-footer__group">
                    <div class="sds-label">{{ section.value.toString }}</div>
                    <div class="sds-footer__links">
                        {%- for page in section.children %}
                            {{ footer.entry(page.url, page.value.toString, '://' in page.url) }}
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {%- endfor %}
            {%- for group in groups %}
                <div class="sds-footer__group">
                    {%- if group.title %}<div class="sds-label">{{ group.title }}</div>{% endif %}
                    <div class="sds-footer__links">
                        {%- for link in group.links %}
                            {{ footer.entry(link.href, link.label, link.external) }}
                        {%- endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="sds-footer__end">
        <span class="sds-mono">{{ soul.product|default(env.projectNode.title)|default('') }}</span>
        {%- if soul.footer.note is defined and soul.footer.note %}
            <span>{{ soul.footer.note }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if env.projectNode.copyright %}
            <span>{{ env.projectNode.copyright }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
        {#- The mark of the service, before its name and never instead of it:
            four glyphs in this system may stand alone and all four say
            something about a result, while a row of bare marks is a row of
            pictures the reader has to already know. Which mark it is comes
            from the URL — see `Brands` — so nothing here can name a service
            the link does not go to, and a host with no mark in the set is the
            label it already was. -#}
        {%- if soul.footer.socials is defined and soul.footer.socials %}
            <span class="sds-row__end">
                {%- for social in soul.footer.socials %}
                    <a class="sds-link sds-link--external" href="{{ social.href }}"
                       target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                        {%- if social.icon %}<sds-icon name="{{ social.icon }}"></sds-icon>{% endif -%}
                        {{ social.label }}</a>
                {%- endfor %}
            </span>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>
</footer>
